  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rwanda Media Programme 2021-25</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Rwanda Media Programme 2021-25</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Media Institute Fojo has applied to the Embassy for funding of MSEK 72  to carry out the &quot;Rwanda Media Programme 2021-25 , Capacity Building and Professionalisation of the Media&quot;. The programme will be implemented in partnership with Swedish Radio Media Development Office (SR MDO). 

The objective of the contribution is to strengthen the independence, professionalism, and sustainability of key actors in the Rwandan media sector with the aim to increase media diversity and media integrity. This in turn will contribute to increase the population&apos;s access to independent, trustworthy, impartial news and information through the media as a platform for citizen&apos;s participation and interaction. The programme activities are divided under three Outcome areas, (1) capacity development of targeted media houses on journalistic capacity, management and financial sustainability, (2) capacity development of Rwanda Broadcasting Agency (RBA) in line with the principles of public service media, and (3) strengthening journalist education in targeted universities.   

The intervention&apos;s total budget is MSEK 78,3, out of which Sida will contribute with MSEK 72 and Swizz Development Cooperation with the part (USD 800 000). Approximately MSEK 32 will be forwarded from Fojo to SR MDO, and about MSEK 14 from Fojo to local implementing partners.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Mediainstitutet Fojo has ans&#xf6;kt om 72 miljoner kronor i st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra insatsen &quot;Rwanda Media Programme 2021-25,  Capacity Building and Professionalisation of the Media&quot; mellan mars 2021 och februari 2026. Insatsen genomf&#xf6;rs i samarbete med Swedish Radio Media Development Office (SR MDO). 

Insatsens m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att st&#xe4;rka oberoende, professionalism och h&#xe5;llbarhet hos media med syftet att &#xf6;ka en m&#xe5;ngfald och integritet i mediasektorn. Detta i sin tur ska bidra till att &#xf6;ka befolkningens tillg&#xe5;ng till oberoende och p&#xe5;litliga nyheter och information genom media och att media p&#xe5; s&#xe5; s&#xe4;tt kan fungera som en plattform f&#xf6;r ansvarsutkr&#xe4;vande och medborgerligt deltagande. Programmet &#xe4;r uppdelat i tre resultatomr&#xe5;den med specifika m&#xe5;l och aktiviteter, (1) kapacitetsst&#xe4;rkande av utvalda mediahus kring journalistisk kapacitet, management och finansiell h&#xe5;llbarhet, (2) kapacitetsst&#xe4;rkande av Rwanda Broadcasting Agency (RBA) i linje med public service-principer, and (3) st&#xe4;rka journalistutbildningen i utvalda universitet.&#xa0; 

Insatsens sammalagda budget &#xe4;r 78,3 miljoner kronor, av vilken Sida finansierar 72 MSEK, och resterande belopp finansieras av den schweitziska ambassaden (800 000 USD). Cirka 32 MSEK kommer vidaref&#xf6;rmedlas till SR MDO och ca 14 MSEK till lokala samarbetpartners.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Overall objective is that the Rwandan people access independent, trustworthy, impartial news and information through the media as a platform for citizens participation and interaction.

The specific objective is strengthening the independence, professionalism, and sustainability of key actors in the Rwandan media sector with the aim to increase media diversity and media integrity.

Outcome 1: Commercial and non-profit media are strengthened to become financially sustainable and to produce and disseminate public interest journalism, reflecting the full composition of society through a balanced presence of women and men, age groups and communities.

Outcome 3: Journalism education institutions have increased skills concerning practical journalism, awareness of gender issues, and are better connected with the Rwandan media and the international journalism community.

The original outcome 2 was formulated as: RBA is strengthened in the process to become an independent, trustworthy and sustainable Public Service Media (PSM) provider according to international journalistic and public service standards. This outcome has been discontinued early 2025 on the initiative of the implementing partner SR MDO. The contribution, hence, remains with the outcome 1 and 3.</narrative>
  </description>
